  "Scenes.Katherine.TalkGangs.CuddlesBothSides": "She walks over and cuddles against you. [say: Problem is I know what it looks like from the other side. A bunch of stuck up assholes who ruin everyone's day just cause they were here before the refugees arrived. Mages who tell everyone what to do but won't tell anyone what they're doing - heck, they barely ever talk to anyone outside the Watch and the aldermen.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Katherine.TalkGangs.NoEasyAnswers": "[say: The short version is that there are no easy answers, at least to Tel'Adre's troubles.] She lets go of you and flops back {0}. [say: Now that you've got me all wound up thinking about the city I hope you're going to help me take my mind off it.]"
  "Scenes.Katherine.TalkGangs.PacesProblemsSame": "She gets up and paces back and forth. [say: All the problems are like that. I can understand why captain {0} drinks and I know why all the city aldermen go gray. Limited food and water, dangerous items that can get into the city, people so lost in lust that they forget to eat - and those are just everyday problems. The city needs people to pull their weight, otherwise the whole place will just turn into a huge orgy and everyone will die of thirst because nobody fixed the pumps that bring water up from the deep aquifer.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Katherine.TalkGangs.SighsDifficultThing": "Kath sighs and then continues, [say: There's a reason everyone says something difficult is like herding cats. We, along with a few other races, tend to be a lot more independent. We're even a little proud that we don't listen to someone just because they say they're in charge. New gangs are always forming because we'd rather follow someone we can see and deal with. Sure, the gang leaders play favorites and take the best food and so on, but at least we know who they are any where it goes. We know who to complain to when things go wrong.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Katherine.TalkGangs.WeirdSometimes": "She shakes her head and says, [say: It can be really weird sometimes. I know why the different gangs are doing what they do and I know why the Watch does what it does. I mean the law about not living in any of the abandoned houses - that makes no sense to anyone living on the street. But it makes a lot of sense to someone working in the Watch. Years ago some gangs fortified buildings and kept the Watch out. The leaders got drunk on power, some became corrupt - or maybe they were a little corrupt to begin with. Anyway, they had to bring in some of the mages to clear them out and lots of innocent people got hurt.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Katherine.TalkHome.AskAboutHome": "You ask Kath about her home and she just beams.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Katherine.TalkHome.FootBrushesYou": "She leans back further and her foot brushes against your {0}. [say: You know, we could be there right now. Just say the word and we could start testing how tight the cords under my bed are.]"
  "Scenes.Katherine.TalkHome.JustTwoRooms": "[pg]I know it's just two little rooms, but it's a slice of paradise next to an alleyway under the open sky.[sayend] "
  "Scenes.Katherine.TalkHome.WalksWhitewashedWalls": "She gets up and walks around the room, drawing her hand across the freshly whitewashed walls. [say: This place is great and I owe it all to you.]"
  "Scenes.Katherine.TalkHome.WonderfulEverything": "[saystart]It's wonderful. It's everything I didn't have out on the street. I have a bed - my own bed! I have a table where I can put together a meal, a wardrobe for my clothes, a big washbasin I can use to bathe whenever I want. But the best thing of all is my door. I can sleep without worrying if someone is going to try to steal my things or worse."
